From 180a136c53c183f8d6ad455d317e6f07d747435e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thang <thang@local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:17:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Gamuroid C1: skin-defined screen boxes through
 gamuroid_screen_layout

New core option gamuroid_screen_layout (declared value 'auto'). The
frontend answers it with
  L1;canvas=WxH;upper=x,y,w,h|none;lower=x,y,w,h|none[;rev=n]
While the value is valid it overrides the screen layout options:
- the output frame is the canvas; uncovered area is black; each visible
  screen is scaled (nearest neighbour) to fill its box, clipped to the
  canvas, the touch screen drawn last;
- the pointer, normalized over the canvas, maps into the lower box; a
  press must start on that box, then clamps to the screen's edge until
  release; no touch while the lower box is hidden; the cursor is drawn
  in the lower box;
- the reported maximum size grows to max(W,H) squared so a rotation is
  only a geometry change; a larger canvas later updates the AV info;
- an invalid value keeps the last valid layout of the session (or the
  configured layouts) and is logged once; 'auto' or empty returns to
  the configured layouts;
- all of this is per session (reset at load and unload) and never
  touches save states.
Parser in gamuroid/screen_layout_value.cpp (no emulator dependency,
unit-tested on the host).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
